waydroid-gralloc-fix upstream tarballs
======================================

This directory carries two upstream source tarballs that the ebuild
consumes via ${FILESDIR} instead of SRC_URI:

    waydroid-minigbm-16844ba.tar.gz  -> android_external_minigbm @
                                        16844babfbd83d7c206ca22256257cbf26ca7de1
    waydroid-libdrm-6bfcfc7.tar.gz   -> android_external_libdrm  @
                                        6bfcfc725fbe0ece0918535556d61ee567b1ffff

The full commit SHAs are pinned in
    ../waydroid-gralloc-fix-1.0.0.ebuild
as MINIGBM_COMMIT and LIBDRM_COMMIT.  The short form in the
filenames above is just for humans.


Why they live here
------------------

See the block above `MINIGBM_COMMIT=` in the ebuild for the failure
that led to this layout.  In short: codeload's branch-head URL
followed upstream HEAD and Manifest byte-checks broke, and pinning
to a SHA in a codeload URL still relies on GitHub's autogenerated
archives staying byte-stable (which the vendor explicitly does
not commit to).  Local files sidestep both.

Long term this is expected to move to a real distfiles mirror
(gs://chromeos-localmirror or a whale-owned bucket).  See the
follow-up captured in the PR that introduced this layout.


Audit procedure
---------------

Because the tarballs are git blobs, `git diff` cannot show their
content and there is no Manifest hash left to compare against.
To convince yourself that the bytes we ship match the pinned
upstream SHAs, unpack them and compare the trees:

    # From the top of a whaleos checkout.
    OVERLAY=src/third_party/chromiumos-overlay
    PKG=$OVERLAY/app-containers/waydroid-gralloc-fix

    # 1) Reference tree from upstream.
    tmp=$(mktemp -d)
    git clone -b lineage-18.1 \
        https://github.com/WayDroid/android_external_minigbm \
        "$tmp/minigbm"
    git -C "$tmp/minigbm" checkout \
        16844babfbd83d7c206ca22256257cbf26ca7de1

    git clone -b lineage-18.1 \
        https://github.com/WayDroid/android_external_libdrm \
        "$tmp/libdrm"
    git -C "$tmp/libdrm" checkout \
        6bfcfc725fbe0ece0918535556d61ee567b1ffff

    # 2) Tree from the committed tarballs.
    tar -C "$tmp" -xzf "$PKG/files/waydroid-minigbm-16844ba.tar.gz"
    tar -C "$tmp" -xzf "$PKG/files/waydroid-libdrm-6bfcfc7.tar.gz"

    # 3) Compare contents (ignore .git/, which upstream ships and
    #    the tarball does not).
    diff -r --exclude=.git \
        "$tmp/android_external_minigbm-16844babfbd83d7c206ca22256257cbf26ca7de1" \
        "$tmp/minigbm"
    diff -r --exclude=.git \
        "$tmp/android_external_libdrm-6bfcfc725fbe0ece0918535556d61ee567b1ffff" \
        "$tmp/libdrm"

Both diffs should report no differences.  If they do, the
tarball was regenerated against a different upstream state and
should be refreshed via the procedure documented at the top of
the ebuild.


Licenses in this directory
--------------------------

* waydroid-minigbm-<sha>.tar.gz:
    Ships its own LICENSE (3-clause BSD, Chromium OS Authors) and
    Android.bp `license_kinds` covering Apache-2.0 / BSD / MIT.
    The tarball's top-level LICENSE is what chromite/licensing's
    licenses_lib.py picks up automatically for this ebuild.

* waydroid-libdrm-<sha>.tar.gz:
    Used only for build-time header references (xf86drm.h etc.).
    No object code from this tarball ends up in our shipped
    libminigbm_gralloc_gbm_mesa.so -- runtime libdrm is provided
    by the container's vendor libdrm.so, and the host side is
    covered by x11-libs/libdrm (which already carries its own
    chromiumos credit entry).  Per-file MIT-style headers apply
    to the tarball contents.

* CMakeLists.txt, arc-toolchain-t-x86-android.cmake,
  arc-toolchain-t-x86_64-android.cmake,
  0001-cros_gralloc-*.patch, 0002-gbm_mesa-*.patch:
    WhaleOS-authored, BSD-3-Clause.  Full text in LICENSE.wrapper.
    The ebuild's src_unpack() copies LICENSE.wrapper into
    ${WORKDIR}/ so it is scanned alongside the upstream LICENSE.